# fixedbugs, defect 324, lane b10-cli, 2026-10-04.
#
# A zero before an `8` or a `9`: `leading_zero` advised the octal reading as
# well, `0o9` for `09`, which is refused, `9` being no octal digit (C refuses
# `09` as an octal constant too). The one reading such a number has is
# decimal, and it is the one fix offered: `9`, `8_1`. The advice is
# `selfhost/number.hero`'s test of defect 324; this brief form shows the
# headline.

function main()
    a = 09     #~ leading_zero
    b = 0_9    #~ leading_zero
    c = 08_1   #~ leading_zero
    print(a, b, c)
